{
  "status": "no_spectral_axis_in_IMAGE_extension",
  "finding": "IMAGE extension of every cutout is a single 2D plane (293x294 for D2 epochs 1-3; 290x292 for D3 epochs 4-5). There is NO spectral cube axis. SPHEREx L2 spectral images are LVF images: each spatial pixel samples ONE wavelength, given per-pixel by the WCS-WAVE lookup table (WAVE-TAB WCS; axes = Wavelength, Bandwidth). A multi-wavelength spectrum of a point source therefore cannot be extracted from a single cutout; building one would require many exposures with the source at different detector positions (spectral mapping), which a single-epoch cutout does not contain. No spectral points are fabricated.",
  "what_is_provided_instead": "Band-integrated (full-detector-band image) aperture photometry per epoch for the comet and 3 field stars, using the identical method to Phase 1 (aperture r=3 native px, annulus 6-10 px, local median background; flux = sum of background-subtracted pixels). Units of flux_sum: MJy/sr * pixel (sum over aperture pixels of MJy/sr values). Also given per epoch: the real effective wavelength the LVF sampled at the object's position (mean of the reprojected WCS-WAVE wavelength map inside the aperture) - one wavelength sample per epoch, NOT a spectrum.",
  "wavelength_mapping": "WCS-WAVE BinTable (X,Y grid over the full 2040x2040 detector + VALUES[2,ny,nx]: [wavelength_um, bandwidth_um]); IMAGE header CTYPE1W/CTYPE2W = WAVE-TAB with PS1_0W/PS2_0W = WCS-WAVE. Wavelength varies smoothly across the detector (LVF gradient); across each 0.5-deg cutout it spans roughly 0.15-0.25 um. NCHANNEL=32, WCHANNEL=64 in header; PSF extension is (121,101,101).",
